# This repository is shared publicly and screen-shared. Everything below is either a
# credential, personal data, or a machine-local identifier that should not leave this laptop.
# Ignoring a file does not redact one already committed — check `git log -p` before assuming.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# All configuration comes from environment variables (CLAUDE.md), which means every real
# value lives in a .env the repo must never see. The .example files are the documentation.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.pfx
*.p12
*.jks
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.asc
*.gpg

# Cloud CLI state. `az login` writes tokens and subscription ids under .azure; azd writes
# the resource ids and any secret app settings of a provisioned environment under .azure/<env>.
.azure/
.aws/
.gcloud/
credentials.json
service-account*.json
*.publishsettings
*.azurePubxml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Candidate data
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This is an applicant tracking system. Every uploaded document is a real person's CV, and a
# CV carries name, address, phone, and employment history. None of it is test data, none of
# it is ours to publish, and a public repo is not a lawful place to store it. Fixtures used
# in tests must be synthetic and named as such.
.media/
media/
uploads/
storage/
*.sqlite3
*.dump
*.sql.gz
db/backups/
tests/fixtures/real/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Our provisioning, not anyone else's
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These record how *this* deployment was built: Azure App Service, a specific subscription's
# per-region VM quota, a domain whose DNS is a Squarespace web form. Someone running on AWS
# or purely locally would be copying decisions that do not apply and inheriting resource
# names, an inbound IP, and a domain verification id that are ours. Kept on disk, not shared.
#
# `docs/decisions/` rather than `docs/`, deliberately: CLAUDE.md places invariants.md,
# data-model.md, and slices.md under docs/, and those are the contract — the files a public
# reader most needs. A blanket docs/ rule would swallow them the day they are moved there,
# and git will not warn you, because it does not descend into an ignored directory to find
# a negation.
infra/
docs/decisions/*

# 0001 is the exception: it establishes the convention rather than recording any deployment,
# names no provider, and CLAUDE.md — which does ship — instructs a reader to record ADRs
# here. Publishing it keeps that instruction true and the directory non-empty. Written as
# `docs/decisions/*` rather than `docs/decisions/` so this negation is reachable at all;
# git does not descend into an ignored directory to evaluate one.
!docs/decisions/0001-record-architecture-decisions.md

# 0008 and 0009 are exceptions for a different reason: neither records a deployment. 0008
# darkens a brand colour that failed the contrast floor the brand book itself sets, and is
# cited from brand/tokens.css, which ships. 0009 explains why the capture endpoint speaks one
# email provider's API instead of the generic transport, and is cited from the capture route,
# which also ships. Holding them back leaves two public files pointing at reasoning nobody
# can read. They name no resource, hostname, region or subscription.
!docs/decisions/0008-ink-muted-darkened-to-meet-the-contrast-floor.md
!docs/decisions/0009-captures-go-to-mailjet.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-local editor state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .vscode/settings.json holds appService.defaultWebAppToDeploy, which is a full ARM resource
# path — it names the Azure subscription id, the resource group, and the site. That is an
# addressing detail for our tenant, not a project setting, and it changes per machine.
# deployment.md tells a contributor how to set deploySubpath for themselves.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.code-workspace
.claude/settings.local.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python — api/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
staticfiles/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node — web/ (web/.gitignore covers the same ground from inside; this is the safety net)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
out/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo/
.vercel/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS and scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
scratch/
tmp/
